{"id":"n2-030","title":"Noun を はじめとして","romaji":"Noun wo hajime to shite","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Expresses 'starting with', 'beginning with', or 'including'.","longExplanation":"The grammar point Noun を はじめとして is used to emphasize a particular item or example along with others. It translates to 'starting with', 'beginning with', or 'including' in English. It is used to present a specific case and imply there are more related items.","formation":"Noun + をはじめとして","examples":[{"jp":"東京をはじめとして、日本にはたくさんの観光スポットがあります。","romaji":"Tōkyō o hajime to shite, Nihon ni wa takusan no kankō supotto ga arimasu.","en":"There are many tourist spots in Japan, starting with Tokyo.","words":[{"surface":"東京","vocabId":"1447690","reading":"とうきょう"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"はじめ","vocabId":"1342540","reading":"はじめ"},{"surface":"として","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"日本","vocabId":"1582710","reading":"にほん"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"たくさん","vocabId":"1415870","reading":"たくさん"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"観光","vocabId":"1214840","reading":"かんこう"},{"surface":"スポット","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あり","vocabId":"1225940","reading":"あり","baseForm":"ある"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[1,2,3]},{"jp":"彼は、ピアノをはじめとして、たくさんの楽器を演奏できます。","romaji":"Kare wa, piano o hajime to shite, takusan no gakki o ensō dekimasu.","en":"He can play many instruments, starting with piano.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ピアノ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"はじめ","vocabId":"1342540","reading":"はじめ"},{"surface":"として","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"たくさん","vocabId":"1415870","reading":"たくさん"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"楽器","vocabId":"1207340","reading":"がっき"},{"su